        "raw": "![Screenshot_20230126-013530|219x500](upload://e9EK6zLkqJaW71Th6ouUwAS43nO.jpeg)\nThe frequency with which Miss Info shuffles her deck tends to make every game feel like a random start; my first attempt felt like she was playing a lost variant deck with eight copies of Diversionary Tactics!☠️\n\nOn my second try, things fell my way a little more, and I was able to start setting up my heroes, with only one or occasionally two Diversion cards promoting Ongoing destruction each round. Once Aminia revealed herself, the heroes shifted gears; Tachyon pounded her with dual Lightspeed Barrages, and Mainstay and Legacy wore her down, until she was in the low single digits. By the time Akashthriya was finally able to play Scatter Seed, there were a dozen seeds in her trash, and the environment immediately became an ally - the end came for M.I. when Strangling Roots was destroyed, and she was the choicest of 3 hp targets.\n\nChallenging, hard fought win in the end.",
